+## Subtopics
+
+### Sheen-based Transparency
+A technique using the 'sheen' and 'sheen tint' parameters in a physically-based rendering (PBR) engine to highlight outlines (e.g., sulci and gyri) without changing object opacity, thus retaining depth information [S3, unofficial]. It applies sheen to capture foldings and crevices on surfaces and increase specular reflection in those areas, while sheen tint controls the colors of the sheen's specular reflections [S3, unofficial]. Unlike reducing surface opacity to see underlying structures, sheen highlights outlines while preserving opacity and depth information [S3, unofficial]. It is used in Horizon's integrated PBR engine to highlight visualization features, such as outlining sulci and gyri of the brain cortex or displaying connectivity networks alongside cortical surfaces [S3, unofficial].
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per sample, as it involves a constant number of arithmetic operations (dot product, additions, clamps) [S2].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary memory per sample [S2].
